---
/** Decision Tool #2 — Annual Maintenance Budget Planner (estimator pattern). */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import SampleNotice from '../../components/SampleNotice.astro';
import RelatedLinks from '../../components/RelatedLinks.astro';
import TrustMeta from '../../components/TrustMeta.astro';

const related = [
  { title: 'Roof Life Expectancy Estimator', href: '/tools/roof-life-expectancy-estimator/', type: 'Decision Tool', description: 'How many years the roof has left — the companion question.' },
  { title: 'Commercial Roof Coatings', href: '/knowledge/roof-coatings/', type: 'Encyclopedia', description: 'The mid-life capital alternative a good budget anticipates.' },
  { title: 'CRI Methodology', href: '/about/methodology/', type: 'Governance', description: 'How every CRI tool is built and validated.' },
];
---

<Base
  title="Maintenance Budget Planner"
  description="CRI's Maintenance Budget Planner is in development and does not yet produce budget ranges. Its methodology is published here for scrutiny while the underlying cost data is validated."
  noindex={true}
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ name: 'Tools', href: '/tools/' }, { name: 'Maintenance Budget Planner' }]} />

  {/* Not indexed: draft methodology. Same rule as the estimator. */}
  <article class="container section--tight">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow" data-pagefind-filter="type">Decision Tool</p>
      <h1>Maintenance Budget Planner</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        In development. This tool does not yet produce budget ranges — its cost rates are
        still pre-validation placeholders. The methodology is published below so it can be
        examined before anyone is asked to trust it.
      </p>
      <TrustMeta updated="2026-07-22" status="draft" />
    </header>

    <SampleNotice status="draft" />

    {/* GATED — the interactive planner is deliberately removed, not hidden, to match the
        Life Expectancy Estimator and the Tools hub's stated standard ("neither will give
        you a number"). Its per-square-foot rates are unvalidated v0.1 placeholders. A tool
        that emits confident dollar ranges from placeholder data, on a contractor-affiliated
        site, fails the same test the estimator's gating documents. Restore the form, the
        result panel, and the calculation script when the CRI cost benchmark dataset (v1.0)
        is validated. The pre-gating implementation is preserved in git history. */}
    <div class="callout callout--caution" style="margin-top: var(--space-5);">
      <strong class="callout__title">In development — not yet validated</strong>
      <p>
        The Maintenance Budget Planner is not currently available, and it will not produce
        a budget range. Its per-square-foot maintenance rates are pre-validation
        placeholders drawn from commonly published planning figures, not from validated
        data. A tool that returns a confident dollar figure from data we have not validated
        would be worse than no tool at all, so it returns nothing.
      </p>
      <p>
        We publish the methodology anyway, in full, below. That is deliberate: you should
        be able to examine and challenge how a tool works <em>before</em> deciding whether
        to trust its output — not after. It is here to be audited, not used.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
        <strong>What to use instead:</strong> a real maintenance budget starts from a
        condition assessment of the specific roof — not from a population-level rate table.
        If you are planning maintenance spending now, start with
        <a href="/knowledge/commercial-roof-inspections/">Commercial Roof Inspections</a>,
        which is published and sourced.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose" style="margin-top: var(--space-7);">
      <h2 id="methodology">Methodology (published for scrutiny — not in operation)</h2>
      <p>
        This is the method the planner <em>will</em> use once its inputs are validated. No
        part of it is running today. The rates below are placeholders: they are plausible,
        they are not yet evidence.
      </p>
      <p>
        The planner multiplies roof area by a per-square-foot annual maintenance rate
        range, adjusted for system and age:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Base rates (placeholder, pre-validation):</strong> single-ply $0.10–$0.25/sf·yr; asphalt multi-ply $0.12–$0.30; metal $0.05–$0.15; coated $0.08–$0.20.</li>
        <li><strong>Age:</strong> 0–5 yrs ×0.7 · 6–15 yrs ×1.0 · 16+ yrs ×1.5.</li>
        <li><strong>Reactive posture:</strong> one-time first-year catch-up allowance of 50–100% of the annual figure, shown separately.</li>
        <li>Results round to sensible increments; ranges are wide by design at v0.1.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These rates are drawn from commonly published industry planning figures and are
        explicitly <strong>unvalidated placeholders</strong> until the CRI cost benchmark
        dataset (v1.0) replaces them — the same standard, and now the same gating, as the
        <a href="/tools/roof-life-expectancy-estimator/">Life Expectancy Estimator</a>.
      </p>
      <h2>What this budget will cover — and won't</h2>
      <p>
        The proactive program: scheduled inspections, drain and housekeeping work, and
        minor repairs. It will not fund capital events (coating cycles, section
        replacement, storm damage) — those are planned separately.
      </p>
      <h2>Limitations</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>National planning ranges; regional labor rates shift them meaningfully.</li>
        <li>Excludes capital events, storm response, and warranty-required specialist work.</li>
        <li>Roofs with chronic defects need a condition assessment before a budget means anything.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </article>

  <RelatedLinks items={related} />
</Base>
